{
  "schema": "plx-search-weights/v1",
  "notes": "Ranking weights live here, never inside the vectors (RISHI-DIRECTION 2.5). retrievers: RRF (or weighted-sum) weight per retriever list. After fusion the top rerank_top candidates are cross-encoder reranked, then final = fused*w_fused + rerank*w_rerank + exact_id*w_exact + authority*w_authority + recency*w_recency (each signal in 0..1; with no reranked candidate w_rerank moves to w_fused). Tuned by python3 -m operating.search.tune; the values below are the hand-set starting point until the eval runs on real chunks. authority: the document priors both paths order by (operating/search/authority.py): plx.documents sorts by their sum plus relevance / the hybrid rank, hybrid adds hybrid_scale x the same sum to its final score. rerank_top, rerank_passage_chars and rerank_timeout_s are the cross-encoder's budget: on the gated eval as a full-read reader (2026-10-31, a loaded host) the rerank of 30 x 1200 characters hit its 4 s time box on every query (p50 = p95 = 4.0 s) and the eval's hybrid gains were made without it, so a rerank that cannot finish in 1.5 s is dropped; on an idle host 20 x 800 characters took 1.6 s and 12 fit the box.",
  "fusion": "rrf",
